WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:07.666
Every time an operator leaves the line to fetch parts, production stops at that station.

00:00:08.266 --> 00:00:12.474
Central stores mean frequent trips, waiting time and crowded aisles.

00:00:12.754 --> 00:00:14.914
Stations run out of parts mid-shift.

00:00:15.194 --> 00:00:20.157
Every trip also adds traffic in the aisles, and increases the chance of accidents.

00:00:20.757 --> 00:00:24.052
A kitting or supply trolley brings the parts to the line.

00:00:24.332 --> 00:00:29.875
Bins are pre-filled with the parts for a job, wheeled to the station, and swapped when empty.

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:34.617
The same trolley can carry kits in the morning and consumables in the afternoon.

00:00:34.897 --> 00:00:38.593
Lock the castors at the station before loading or unloading.

00:00:39.193 --> 00:00:45.622
A Furnisys Link Trolley takes bin rails, pegboards and angled shelves, on four 5 inch castors,

00:00:45.622 --> 00:00:46.649
two with locks.

00:00:46.929 --> 00:00:53.528
An electrical components maker uses one to carry kits to packing stations and restock consumables,

00:00:53.528 --> 00:00:55.144
cutting trips to stores.

00:00:55.744 --> 00:00:57.172
Bring the parts to the people.

00:00:57.452 --> 00:01:00.172
How many trips does your line make to stores each day?

00:01:00.452 --> 00:01:04.050
Comment below, and next, see how packing stations are set up.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:08.895
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

